Palindrome Permutation | HashSet | O(n)

Problem Statement

Given a string s, determine whether any permutation of the string can form a palindrome.

Return true if at least one permutation is a palindrome; otherwise, return false.

Examples
Input: "aab"
Output: true
Explanation: "aba"

Input: "code"
Output: false

Input: "carerac"
Output: true
Explanation: "racecar"


Local IntelliJ Solution:

import java.util.HashSet;
import java.util.Set;

public class PalindromePermutation {

    public static boolean canFormPalindrome(String s){
        Set<Character> set = new HashSet<>();

        for(char ch : s.toCharArray()){
            if(set.contains(ch)){
                set.remove(ch);
            } else {
                set.add(ch);
            }
        }
        return set.size()<=1;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args){
        System.out.println(canFormPalindrome("aab"));//true
        System.out.println(canFormPalindrome("code"));//false
        System.out.println(canFormPalindrome("carerac"));//true
    }
}



=============================================================================================================================================================================
Approach (HashSet)

Observation

A palindrome has the following property:

  ->Every character must occur an even number of times.
  ->At most one character can occur an odd number of times (the middle character).

Instead of storing the frequency of every character, we can keep track of characters that currently have an odd count.

=============================================================================================================================================================================
Algorithm:

1) Create an empty HashSet.
2) Traverse each character in the string.
3) If the character is already present in the set, remove it.
4) Otherwise, add it to the set.
5) After processing all characters:
      If the set size is 0 or 1, a palindrome permutation is possible.
      Otherwise, it is not possible.
